### DocExtract — Ingest e2e requests
### Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the IntelliJ HTTP Client.
### Prerequisites: see e2e/README.md

@host = https://dms.local
@contextPath = /dms
@baseUrl = {{host}}{{contextPath}}
# dvelop-mock's identityprovider-validate.json accepts any bearer token.
@authHeader = Bearer {{$processEnv DMS_TEST_TOKEN}}

@repositoryId = 7cd5d582-2b5d-5e56-9a15-619f94e6e3ed
@documentPropertyValue = testvalue

### Show version
GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: {{authHeader}}

### Upload a document to chunk
# See doc/api/dvelop-dmsapp.yaml, operationId: uploadBlobChunk.
# First POST goes to /blob/chunk; the Location header returned here is the
# contentLocationUri to use for any subsequent chunk (uploaded sequentially).
# @name uploadChunk
POST {{baseUrl}}/r/{{repositoryId}}/blob/chunk
Authorization: {{authHeader}}
Content-Type: application/octet-stream

< ../../e2e/fixtures/letter.txt

### Store the document with properties
# @name storeDocument
POST {{baseUrl}}/r/{{repositoryId}}/o2m/
Accept: application/json
Authorization: {{authHeader}}
Content-Type: application/json
Content-Language: de

{
  "filename": "testfile.pdf",
  "sourceCategory": "DBUE",
  "sourceId": "/dms/r/{{repositoryId}}/source",
  "contentLocationUri": "{{uploadChunk.response.headers.Location}}",
  "sourceProperties": {
    "properties": [
      {
        "key": "1",
        "values": [
          "{{documentPropertyValue}}"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

### Read Object Definitions
# See doc/api/dvelop-dmsapp.yaml, operationId: getObjectDefinitions.
GET {{baseUrl}}/r/{{repositoryId}}/objdef
Authorization: {{authHeader}}

### Get Value List for a Property
# this is an inoffical endpoint for fetching value lists for a specific property.
@dmsPropertyId = 15

POST {{baseUrl}}/r/{{repositoryId}}/validvalues/p/{{dmsPropertyId}}
Authorization: {{authHeader}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": 1,
  "objectDefinitionId": "DREC",
  "remarks": {},
  "multivalueExtendedProperties": {},
  "extendedProperties": {
    "4": "2026-10-04",
    "15": "suchfilter"
  }
}
 